## Write

Answer with one JSON object in the shape below and nothing else.

Voice: plain, short, friendly. Sentence case. No hype. The person scans the text in a few seconds, so keep each sentence under 15 words with one fact in it. Cut filler such as "it looks like", "you may want to", "this is a" or "worth a look", and do not explain what a product or tool does. The left bar already shows each label and signal, so do not repeat them in longer words. Use the words the person sees in PostHog. Never an em dash or an en dash; use a comma or a new sentence. Never quote customer text, never name customers or people, and never name a time of day: the page greets the person itself and the text stays up for hours.

- `headline`: one sentence that counts the items, for example "Three reports need your input".
- `paragraphs`: one or two short paragraphs in item order, at most {{ max_words }} words in total, each a list of segments `{"text", "item_key", "highlight"}`. The first sentence is the top item: what it is and why it matters, nothing more. Every other item gets one short sentence that says what to do or the one fact that matters. Two related items may share a sentence. Never list items ("Also ready: X, Y and Z") and never start a sentence with "Also".
- A linked segment names exactly one item through its `item_key`: a natural phrase of at most {{ max_link_words }} words that starts with a word. Link every item exactly once. Only the top item has `highlight` true. Plain text segments have `item_key` null and `highlight` false, and carry their own spaces.
- `items`: one entry for each item in <items>, in the same order:
  - `key`: the item's key, exactly as given.
  - `label`: at most {{ max_label_words }} words that say what it is.
  - `signal`: the short fact that makes it matter, at most {{ max_signal_chars }} characters. Examples: "Waits for your input", "P1, fix ready", "P0, nobody owns it".

```json
{
  "headline": "string",
  "paragraphs": [[{"text": "string", "item_key": "string or null", "highlight": false}]],
  "items": [{"key": "string", "label": "string", "signal": "string"}]
}
```
